[42.863451, "o", "python -m sysdiag.cli --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[42.892323, "o", "usage: cli.py [-h] [--output OUTPUT] [--db-config DB_CONFIG] [--export-config PATH]\r\n\r\nSystem Diagnostics Exporter\r\n\r\noptions:\r\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\r\n  --output OUTPUT, -o OUTPUT\r\n                        Destination path for diagnostics report JSON\r\n  --db-config DB_CONFIG\r\n                        Path to database configuration file\r\n  --export-config PATH  Export the resolved active configuration snapshot to PATH as JSON\r\n"]
[42.897146, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@44f94e080ce4:/app/repo# "]
[60.809041, "i", "cat > README.md <<'MD'\n# sysdiag\n\n`sysdiag` is an internal systems diagnostics and operational reporting tool.\nIt gathers system resource information, network reachability, and database health\nmetrics to assist in infrastructure triage.\n\n## Usage\n\nWrite the default diagnostics report to `/var/diagnostics/report.json`:\n\n```bash\nsysdiag\n```\n\nWrite a diagnostics report to a custom path:\n\n```bash\nsysdiag --output /var/diagnostics/report.json\n```\n\nUse a custom database configuration file:\n\n```bash\nsysdiag --db-config /path/to/database.conf\n```\n\nExport the active resolved configuration snapshot as JSON while still writing the\ndiagnostics report:\n\n```bash\nsysdiag --db-config /path/to/database.conf --export-config /tmp/sysdiag-config.json\n```\n\nSensitive values such as passwords, tokens, and API keys are redacted from the\nexported configuration snapshot.\nMD\npython -m compileall -q sysdiag\npython -m sysdiag.cli --output /tmp/sysdiag-report-2.json --db-config etc/database.conf --export-config /tmp/sysdiag-config-2.json\n"]
[60.80918, "i", "python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor path in ('/tmp/sysdiag-report-2.json', '/tmp/sysdiag-config-2.json'):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        data = json.load(f)\n    print(path, sorted(data.keys()))\nprint('database report keys:', sorted(json.load(open('/tmp/sysdiag-report-2.json'))['database'].keys()))\nPY\n"]
[60.810394, "o", "cat > README.md <<'MD'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # sysdiag\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
